var PEOPLE=[{"g":"p1","name":"Alanna Carruthers","title":"Associate Director, Client Success","co":"ICUC, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/alanna-carruthers-1159b364/","past":"12 years at ICUC, starting as a Content Specialist moderating brands' social channels, then Project Coordinator leading a content team, then Customer Success Manager for pharma clients. Earlier: publicity intern at FLIP Publicity (NXNE, Luminato, Pan Am Games) and two years teaching in London, UK.","edu":"Western University, BA Communication and Media Studies; Centennial College, corporate communications and PR","about":"A communications and PR professional who has managed teams of 10 to 20 people and high-profile clients. In her current role she works with ICUC's growth, strategy and insights leaders to shape social media solutions, advises client executives, and supports new business pitches.","qs":["You started at ICUC moderating social channels and are now an Associate Director. What did you do differently at each step that got you promoted?","What does a client success team do at a social media agency, and how is it different from account management at a creative agency?","You've managed pharma clients, where every post is regulated. How do you keep social work creative when the rules are that tight?","When you hire a junior team member, what skills or habits make someone stand out?","You studied communications and PR. How did that background help you, and what did you have to learn on the job?"]},{"g":"p1","name":"Karishma Wadia","title":"Copywriter","co":"Dentsu Creative, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/karishmawadia/","past":"Copywriter at Mosaic North America (McCain, Google, Hershey, RBC, Budweiser) and Zulu Alpha Kilo (Subaru, Bell, Interac, Whirlpool). Two copywriting internships at Ogilvy Mumbai.","edu":"Humber College, Graduate Certificate in Advertising Copywriting; York University, Post Graduate Certificate in Digital and Content Marketing","about":"Writes for Honda, Acura, Taco Bell, Nespresso, Maison Perrier and Subway at Dentsu Creative. Cannes Lions 30 Under 30 Creative Academy 2025 (scholarship), Adweek Creative 100 with her art director partner Michelle Meng, and Campaign Canada 30 Under 30. She has spoken on Campaign Canada's podcast about moving from India to Canada and building a network with zero cultural context.","qs":["You moved from India to Canada and had to build a network from scratch. What actually worked for you in your first year?","How did you put together your portfolio coming out of Humber, and what in it got you hired at Zulu Alpha Kilo?","You and Michelle Meng work as a creative team. How did you find each other, and how do you split the work on a brief?","What was the Cannes Lions Creative Academy like, and how should a student prepare to apply for scholarships like it?","On a project like Honda Carstumes, how does an idea get from the first brainstorm to something the client buys?"]},{"g":"p1","name":"Michelle Meng","title":"Art Director","co":"Dentsu Creative, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/michelle-meng/","past":"Art Director at Mosaic North America after an internship there (Wonder Bread, YouTube x NBA, PC Financial, Coffee Mate, Peloton). She art directed the RITZ #WelcomeNewFlavors campaign. Art director intern at Juniper Park\\TBWA (CIBC).","edu":"McGill University, Marketing; Miami Ad School Toronto, Art Direction program","about":"A marketing graduate who moved into art direction through Miami Ad School. ADWEEK Creative 100 with her partner Karishma Wadia, Campaign Canada 30 Under 30, and a 2026 LIA Creative LIAisons mentee. She has said her Canadian Chinese background gives her a different set of eyes, and she likes to bring both East and West into her work.","qs":["You studied marketing at McGill and then went to ad school for art direction. When did you know you wanted to switch to the creative side?","What did Miami Ad School give you that a marketing degree didn't?","You went from intern to art director at Mosaic. What helped you make that jump?","How does your own background show up in your work, like on the RITZ #WelcomeNewFlavors campaign?","What should a junior art director's portfolio show today, and how do you use tools like Procreate or AI in your process?"]},{"g":"p1","name":"AJ Braysher","title":"Strategy Manager","co":"dentsu, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/braysher/","past":"5+ years at dentsu, from Client Executive at Carat Perth (Mastercard, Crown Resorts) to Digital Manager, then Media Effectiveness Manager and Product Lead in Toronto for national automotive brands. Earlier: digital strategist at Multiplier Media and content strategist for a Sky News Business show in Australia. B&T 30 Under 30 finalist and AdNews Young Gun.","edu":"Deakin University, Graduate Certificate in Marketing","about":"A media strategist working out what media strategy looks like for the next generation, with a lot of building with AI. He represented Canada at dentsu's global AI summit in Tokyo. His path is unusual: he started at 15 editing video for YouTubers, spent years DJing, then moved through media, analytics and strategy in Australia and Canada.","qs":["You started editing video for YouTubers at 15 and DJed for years. How did that lead into media strategy?","You moved with dentsu from Perth to Toronto. How did that happen, and what was different about Canadian media?","What AI tools do you actually build for your team, and what should a student learn to be useful with AI on day one?","How is a strategy manager's job different from a media planner's?","You were at dentsu's AI summit in Tokyo. What is one change coming for media jobs in the next few years?"]},{"g":"p1","name":"Sandeep Kahlon","title":"Digital Account Director","co":"Carat and dentsu X, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandeep-kahlon-2b43011a/","past":"Lead Strategist and Supervisor at dentsu X (Jaguar, Land Rover, Bosch Home Appliances), after Senior Media Strategist (Sabra, CDIC, Dairy Queen). Before that at DentsuBos as Digital Investment Planner and Communication Coordinator (Lexus dealers, Constellation Brands). He spent 10 years as an operations manager at an A&W franchise before starting in advertising.","edu":"Ryerson University (now Toronto Metropolitan University)","about":"Turns client goals into digital tactics, with a focus on consumer data research. He has led media strategy for automotive and home appliance brands and coaches junior staff on omnichannel advertising. On the panel he wants to share lessons learned and advice for people starting out.","qs":["You spent ten years running an A&W restaurant before advertising. What made you switch, and what from that job still helps you?","You've stayed in the dentsu network for more than ten years. How did you move from coordinator to account director?","How do you train junior planners, and what mistakes do you see new people make most?","On accounts like Jaguar and Land Rover, how do you decide which digital channels get the budget?","What does a digital account director do day to day that a student wouldn't guess?"]},{"g":"p2","name":"Japnit Kaur","title":"Media Planner","co":"WPP Media, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/japnitkaur1/","past":"Digital Analyst at Tata Consultancy Services on the BMO account, sales associate at UNIQLO, marketing coordinator intern at Sant Diaries, and audit associate at KPMG before moving into media.","edu":"York University, postgraduate certificates in Public Relations, Advertising and Applied Communication, and in Digital and Content Marketing","about":"A marketing and communications professional with a passion for social media analytics, content marketing and storytelling, who has created content reaching 10K+ users a week. She joined WPP Media in December 2025 and credits her managers and mentors there for giving her the chance.","qs":["You worked in audit at KPMG and as an analyst on BMO before media. How did you make the switch into media planning?","What did you do to land the job at WPP Media, and who helped you along the way?","You did two postgraduate certificates at York. Which parts did you actually use in your first planning job?","What does your first year as a media planner look like day to day?","For students working retail jobs while studying, how can that experience help them get into advertising?"]},{"g":"p2","name":"Kate Newell","title":"Customer Success Manager","co":"Spotify, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kate-newell-088b001b4/","past":"Strategist at OMD Canada before joining Spotify in 2025. Internships in communications consulting at Collective Culture + Communication (WestJet, LifeWorks rebrand) and in marketing at Collective Beauty Brands, where she worked on a brand's Instagram launch and influencer selection.","edu":"Trinity College Dublin, MSc Digital Marketing Strategy (dissertation on TikTok as a marketing tool for small businesses reaching Gen Z); Western University, BA Media, Information and Technoculture","about":"Kate moved from the agency side (OMD) to the platform side (Spotify), where she works with advertisers on Spotify's ad products. She is also a mentor at Student Day.","qs":["You moved from strategist at OMD to customer success at Spotify. How is working at a platform different from working at an agency?","What does a customer success manager at Spotify do for advertisers?","You did a master's in Dublin. Was it worth it, and would you recommend studying abroad for a marketing career?","Your dissertation was about TikTok and Gen Z. What did you find, and do you still use it?","What should a student know about audio and podcast advertising before they apply?"]},{"g":"p2","name":"Katrina Thorn","title":"Account Manager","co":"MIK Studio, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/katrina-thorn/","past":"Senior Producer, Brand Production at Canva and Localization Producer for Canva Design School. Senior Producer at Shutterstock Custom (Walmart, McDonald's, L'Oréal, Amazon), where she led the HIV in View photo and video shoots in six countries. National Content Producer for iHeartRadio at Bell Media. Content operations at TELUS, and promotions at Corus.","edu":"Ryerson University (now TMU), BA Radio and Television Arts; The Chang School of Continuing Education","about":"A creative operations and program leader with 15+ years managing marketing and content work across media and tech companies. Her strengths are client partnership, project leadership, and building workflows that let global teams deliver at scale.","qs":["You've worked at Corus, TELUS, Bell Media, Shutterstock, Canva and now MIK Studio. How did you decide when it was time to move?","What does a producer actually do on a shoot like HIV in View, across six countries?","You moved from producing into account management. What is the difference between the two roles?","What did working remotely for a global company like Canva teach you?","For a student interested in production or creative operations, where is a good place to start?"]},{"g":"p2","name":"Aakash Singhal","title":"Account Manager","co":"GumGum, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/aakashsinghal7/","past":"Programmatic Solutions Manager at GumGum. Client Success Manager and Programmatic Strategist at StackAdapt. Programmatic Coordinator, Trading Strategy at GroupM on the Ford account. Earlier he taught a cinema program in Durham schools. He is also Director of Communications and a board member at AdClub of Toronto.","edu":"Durham College, Advertising and Marketing Communications, and a postgraduate in Advanced Filmmaking; Symbiosis International University, MA; University of Mumbai, Bachelor of Mass Media, Advertising","about":"Uses AI and contextual intelligence to run programmatic campaigns, with experience on both the agency trading desk and the DSP side. He attended AdClub Student Day in 2019 as a student and calls it the launchpad for his career, where he met the mentors who shaped his path.","qs":["You sat in the audience at Student Day in 2019. What did you do at that event that helped your career?","You've worked at an agency trading desk, a DSP and an ad tech vendor. How do the jobs differ, and which would you recommend first?","In plain words, what is contextual advertising, and why does it matter now that cookies are going away?","You studied filmmaking too. How does that creative background help you in programmatic?","How do you follow up with someone you meet at an event like this without being awkward?"]},{"g":"m","name":"Micheal Bispo","title":"Director, Media Effectiveness & Planning","co":"OLG, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/michealbispo/","past":"SVP Growth and Marketing at Omnicom Media Group Canada (OMD, PHD, Hearts & Science, Touché!). Consultant to Loblaw's CMO, where he helped stand up the Loblaw Media retail media network. Director of Brand Media Strategy at Rogers ($150M+ in paid media). At Dentsu Aegis he launched the Vizeum agency in Canada and later led the P&G Canada account.","edu":"MacEwan University, Diploma in Advertising and Public Relations","about":"Works where data, technology, media strategy and commerce meet. At OLG he reports to the CMO, built the enterprise measurement framework, and restructured how the company works with agencies. He also founded a consulting practice, and judges the CMA Awards and Media Innovation Awards.","qs":["You've worked at agencies, at a holding company, as a consultant and now at a brand. Which seat taught you the most?","What does media effectiveness mean in simple terms, and how do you prove that advertising worked?","You helped Loblaw launch a retail media network. What is retail media, and why is everyone talking about it?","You started with a college diploma. What would you tell a student who worries about not having a university degree?","When you judge awards like the CMA Awards, what makes a piece of work stand out?"]},{"g":"m","name":"Karen Geller","title":"Sr. Director, In House Media Agency","co":"Corus Entertainment","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/karen-geller-85022563/","past":"Almost 20 years in the Corus in-house agency, starting as a media planner at Alliance Atlantis and working up to Director through mergers with Canwest and Shaw Media. Senior Manager of Media and Connections Planning at Diageo, then back to Corus as Sr. Director. Earlier: Senior Media Executive at MBS Media Buying Services.","edu":"York University, BA Psychology; Humber College, Post Graduate Diploma (Honours) in Advertising Media Sales","about":"Experienced in media planning, broadcast buying and digital media, and describes herself as both a thinker and a doer. She also teaches marketing and advertising as a contract professor at Seneca Polytechnic.","qs":["You studied psychology before advertising. How does that help you plan media?","You stayed through several mergers at the same in-house agency. What did you learn about building a career through big company changes?","What is an in-house media agency, and how is it different from working at an agency like OMD or Carat?","You went from Corus to Diageo and back. What did working on the brand side teach you?","As a professor at Seneca, what do you wish students knew before their first media job?"]},{"g":"m","name":"Baris Ozmorali","title":"Senior Account Manager","co":"MIK Studio, Toronto","li":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/barisozmorali/","past":"Account Manager at MIK Studio before his promotion. Project Manager at WeFX on work for Marvel, Apple, Netflix and the Roku Channel. Scheduling and engineering coordinator for live NBA, NHL and MLB broadcasts at Dome Productions.","edu":"Toronto Metropolitan University, Bachelor's in Production, Business Essentials; Google project management certificates","about":"Leads large North American accounts at MIK Studio, mainly with Spotify, and has run 30+ projects at once with teams across North America, Europe and Au